==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|un|consciously}}, and more rarely, from {{suffix|en|unconscious|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˌʌnˈkɑnʃəsli/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-unconsciously.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˌʌnˈkɒnʃəsli/}}
* {{hyph|en|un|con|scious|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In an [[unconscious]] manner; [[unknowingly]]
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1831|author={{w|Letitia Elizabeth Landon}}|title=Romance and Reality|volume=3|page=246|text=Emily had thought she was accustomed to consider Lorraine attached to another; but that vague hope which lingers so '''unconsciously''' in the human heart, or not so much hope as uncertainty, that had as yet given no tangible shape to her rival, had ill prepared her to find that rival in her own familiar companion.}}

